**Next steps after wave 1** — Wave 1 left high-severity gaps: X-ray literature table blocked by DNS/budget (only built-in Roach+2020/Dessert+2020 used) and production-mechanism survey without quotes or Viel+2005 translation; BBN baseline offset and DW normalization unresolved with server caps not enforced. Reopening d-08/d-09 with reduced scope (<=400-point grids, 5-6 X-ray points, verbatim quotes via read_arxiv_chunk/cite, local dispatch) directly addresses those blocks, while two new tool-quantifiable directions resolve DW Omega=0.12 normalization vs Abazajian Eq.37 and BBN Delta N_eff robustness to Yp/D/H and thermalization, enabling a combined BBN+X-ray viable-region map in the final wave within 40-call/36-min budget.

New lines of investigation: Cross-check DW relic-density normalization and map Omega_s h2=0.12 contour vs BBN+X-ray exclusion; Quantify BBN Delta N_eff bound robustness to Yp/D/H baselines and thermalization fraction (BBN vs CMB).
